The utility displays the contents of or, by default, its standard
input,  to  the  standard  output.  The display begins at a byte,
line or 512‐byte block location in the input.  Numbers  having  a
leading  plus  (‘‘+’’)  sign are relative to the beginning of the
input, for example, starts the display at the second byte of  the
input.   Numbers  having  a  leading minus (‘‘‐’’) sign or no ex‐
plicit sign are relative to the end of the  input,  for  example,
displays  the  last two lines of the input.  The default starting
location is or the last 10 lines of the input.  The  options  are
